"q-140563" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ in $Ax=b$ given that the matrix $A$ is orthogonal, and \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15} & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} & \\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nHence, since $A$ is orthogonal, we have ${A}^{-1}={A}^{T}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}Ax & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485529 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da20ffe7-173b-5fc0-8629-3b9b70222860" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5926b979-2296-5e06-b854-1498d765329c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485018} {:answer/id #uuid "887a1bd2-c587-5e95-a0cc-d565e244878d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485114} {:answer/id #uuid "9f356501-6df9-5979-9372-357a6a302ea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485161} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b65862-95be-58c5-99d4-ab0f73d0d20a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485213} {:answer/id #uuid "d13939e6-36f9-5572-80e9-e753d41ea7a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f356501-6df9-5979-9372-357a6a302ea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485161} :answer-field/id #uuid "70e8c2d5-fce1-5f92-9639-37c01a107aaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4cd1f663-1b26-5239-80df-41dfbaf9dd53" :question/math-academy-id "q-140564" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the orthogonal matrix $Q?$\n\nI. ${Q}^{2}$ is orthogonal\n\nII. $Q$ is a diagonal matrix\n\nIII. $Q-I$ is invertible" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the product ${Q}^{2}\\cdot ({Q}^{2})^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{2}\\cdot ({Q}^{2})^{T} & =(Q\\cdot Q)\\cdot (Q\\cdot Q)^{T} \\\\  & =(Q\\cdot Q)\\cdot ({Q}^{T}\\cdot {Q}^{T}) \\\\  & =Q\\cdot (Q\\cdot {Q}^{T})\\cdot {Q}^{T} \\\\  & =Q(I){Q}^{T} \\\\  & =Q{Q}^{T} \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix:\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$Q$ is an orthogonal matrix, but it is not a diagonal matrix.\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $Q=I$ be the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix. Then, \n\n$$\nQ-I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe $2\\times 2$  zero matrix, which is not an invertible matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272134 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da20ffe7-173b-5fc0-8629-3b9b70222860" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98311a5d-c789-50b1-998c-82789cf3e15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464132} {:answer/id #uuid "4a1caad2-1552-53b2-ad65-0faf937f9cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a1caad2-1552-53b2-ad65-0faf937f9cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464133} :answer-field/id #uuid "94d3e7a6-f070-518f-bca6-72c0a2e523f0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465000} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2950a552-7b64-54f3-9df5-37fbc1daf708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464134} {:answer/id #uuid "57bc0bcf-2d74-5b42-80b8-a9462aac80d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2950a552-7b64-54f3-9df5-37fbc1daf708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464134} :answer-field/id #uuid "11e24475-4728-5731-901b-4204e0ce6cef" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465001} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "427e5f77-75e3-5ea5-8f93-8f5a66733617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464136} {:answer/id #uuid "01222f75-c4bd-542d-8467-b02dd4c8ea9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "427e5f77-75e3-5ea5-8f93-8f5a66733617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464136} :answer-field/id #uuid "d74724c4-d89e-52f6-b857-07eecbd822cb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a3d61daa-c943-5ecf-a98c-7f9bcd210491" :question/math-academy-id "q-140565" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the $n\\times n$ orthogonal matrix $Q$ and the $n\\times n$ matrix $P?$\n- **I.** If $\\lambda $ is a real eigenvalue of $Q,$ then $\\lambda =\\pm 1$\n- **II.** If the determinant of $P$ is either $1$ or $-1,$ then $P$ is orthogonal\n- **III.** $Q-I$ is singular\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If $\\lambda $ is an eigenvalue of an orthogonal matrix $Q$ then $\\lambda =\\pm 1$\n\n- Statement II is false. Every orthogonal matrix has the determinant equal to $\\pm 1$, but not every matrix with the determinant equal to $\\pm 1$ is orthogonal. As a counterexample, consider the following matrix:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe determinant of $P$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P)=2\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 1=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n however, $P$ is not orthogonal since, for example, the first column is not normalized.\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, consider the following orthogonal matrix:\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\nQ-I=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & -\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand $Q-I$ is not singular since, for example, it doesn't have proportional rows or columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485551 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "013b5339-64c6-5007-b26d-8e17a9af1e89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484818} {:answer/id #uuid "7c5f1870-fd22-5be7-af97-1d34504dc1ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485087} {:answer/id #uuid "a1ab3e2b-fed0-5981-a65e-df0e8c2ddfca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485168} {:answer/id #uuid "e8926bb3-412f-5849-81bb-0a7971aa7025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485308} {:answer/id #uuid "eede04ef-d603-58e9-897e-2826d2f2ca05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8926bb3-412f-5849-81bb-0a7971aa7025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485308} :answer-field/id #uuid "d87ebbb7-74a3-5ba5-93e4-063a3206f479" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83aaff63-f033-5323-bd52-af10976e5a16" :question/math-academy-id "q-177656" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fff5188-49f9-5ba0-bde2-420c0a8bf40b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484850} {:answer/id #uuid "5ceae71f-3b25-523c-b399-ef203fc61915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485024} {:answer/id #uuid "65bb6b5a-1475-52a9-b0fc-a90761104b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485039} {:answer/id #uuid "74086728-2a15-558c-9eda-23ae9a3e855c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485067} {:answer/id #uuid "fb3b08e9-1bbb-5ff8-b3a8-ba094835416d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb3b08e9-1bbb-5ff8-b3a8-ba094835416d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485356} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9f3276f-779b-51ad-9d6b-890a9e89a2ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46db878d-0e5d-50fb-979a-d499bbe2ee60" :question/math-academy-id "q-177659" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{24}{25} \\\\ \\frac{24}{25} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A\\cdot {A}^{T}\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2885a8f4-fb03-536b-9311-dfd70502c16e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484891} {:answer/id #uuid "658947d8-f94a-5959-8f98-7a5a5937a024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485038} {:answer/id #uuid "c5808f66-f6df-524e-9eaa-c92ca8711d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485241} {:answer/id #uuid "d001edcd-7aa6-5ff6-a64d-f2057575b857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485256} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb3e8ee-7783-5420-882a-066010a26592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2885a8f4-fb03-536b-9311-dfd70502c16e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484891} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f1d3ef9-793b-5e24-8e99-68db383cf524" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb8ec734-9246-5393-99e6-34bea8046fc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-177661" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b83cbcb7-0b07-5ebc-aa53-89e2be0b52df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450114} {:answer/id #uuid "a563d8ec-88fc-5fd2-9125-f7a62ee49b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a563d8ec-88fc-5fd2-9125-f7a62ee49b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450115} :answer-field/id #uuid "f129ca4a-c8e7-580b-91d4-1a0d29e6e4ed" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dda02671-8980-5223-a56e-89f2f6a71af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450116} {:answer/id #uuid "72a3e0ac-77bc-591c-8e67-8888858b7e84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dda02671-8980-5223-a56e-89f2f6a71af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450116} :answer-field/id #uuid "e642ba26-55cc-5b02-a022-90bbe00ce622" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451012} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80c70086-78d0-561d-add7-060ea37b84aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450118} {:answer/id #uuid "990655aa-5186-5262-8a17-20c96c8aacfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80c70086-78d0-561d-add7-060ea37b84aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450118} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d44e42c-bf19-521c-a0c4-c2026051681e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ef1bd48-9355-501c-9dc0-0c7250b226e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-177663" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is a square matrix\n- **II.** $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n- **III.** $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A\\cdot {A}^{T}\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24b180b5-cbd5-5b9a-ae2d-e655faa840d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484884} {:answer/id #uuid "2bad9be6-a82c-5f4f-879d-dcbfb4a2f3c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484905} {:answer/id #uuid "bae5ca7d-1994-5c77-8acf-ebf9f1ba4fb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485218} {:answer/id #uuid "e09075e8-f3b4-55d6-af6b-f159bb382010" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485291} {:answer/id #uuid "f4ed5811-580e-5ab7-9782-e45b658d4380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4ed5811-580e-5ab7-9782-e45b658d4380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485340} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bb63660-4233-5926-a45a-b277379f4cec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "203918fb-bff3-5640-9116-ee4c833a081b" :question/math-academy-id "q-177668" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is a square matrix\n\nII. ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I$\n\nIII. $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. The number of rows in $A$ is not the same as the number of columns. So, it's not a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\cdot A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not a square matrix and ${A}^{T}\\cdot A\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a22cfc-9a78-57ab-93a4-3c3255c34bf7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Inverse of an Orthogonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40815aa7-1131-5c98-b1ca-d06d1ce86431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484957} {:answer/id #uuid "8504229e-0026-5df9-835e-7fe9e313f2ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485104} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7e2b55-2e48-5a32-bdcc-b4982d78bb17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485185} {:answer/id #uuid "d8eeb0b4-6fde-5e11-820c-fd3ac0790bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485271} {:answer/id #uuid "e6941f8d-a51c-5dea-b565-f989e9b10972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa7e2b55-2e48-5a32-bdcc-b4982d78bb17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485185} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1b3bc70-0e0f-5fed-8f78-181f20b95555" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ab7c31a0-8694-52ae-9c85-3e23bf4389e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-39867" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ in $Ax=b$ given that the matrix $A$ is orthogonal, and \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nHence, since $A$ is orthogonal, we have ${A}^{-1}={A}^{T}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}Ax & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134244 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133949 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee00be0e-f6a2-5269-a36d-1eeaf1b32344" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Product of Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb197d48-db10-5005-a643-6196a02e7f5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131505} {:answer/id #uuid "09fc5509-0fe6-5a43-83a3-eb571792902d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131507} {:answer/id #uuid "0ea43c74-a7de-5495-88c7-0382f008fbb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131508} {:answer/id #uuid "20045821-316a-5633-acd8-365f31e8c083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484876} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0f3828-98fe-56d1-a565-afe9f584dd2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb197d48-db10-5005-a643-6196a02e7f5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131505} :answer-field/id #uuid "31fbdaad-a6a3-563a-99d3-49ed8677de91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33946d4e-a787-5aee-914d-44804d2c4a75" :question/math-academy-id "q-39872" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}| \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134245 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133949 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee00be0e-f6a2-5269-a36d-1eeaf1b32344" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Product of Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81b820cb-72ef-50ef-a9bf-f5e8a38636e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131510} {:answer/id #uuid "e8f6bb18-184a-5a98-bdf2-32973baa82c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131512} {:answer/id #uuid "26532a6d-633c-526a-a3c4-ae6120b78154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}-26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484887} {:answer/id #uuid "36d6ba13-23fd-551d-9a3a-a0cf24d03ce2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}+26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484933} {:answer/id #uuid "53f9636f-f836-5a16-b4fe-9bd98143b7eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}+32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8f6bb18-184a-5a98-bdf2-32973baa82c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131512} :answer-field/id #uuid "219dc850-1ff5-58e7-b926-bbc34284f736" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "48e38c7e-484d-5cb3-85cb-dfcc3bab8451" :question/math-academy-id "q-39873" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 8 \\\\ -4 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-8\\cdot (-4)| \\\\  & =34\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a22cfc-9a78-57ab-93a4-3c3255c34bf7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Inverse of an Orthogonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01ceb64c-0881-5a66-b48f-18aa35dc7f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484820} {:answer/id #uuid "2ce8b058-46a3-588d-b171-a5e100cbc0ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484909} {:answer/id #uuid "af25de84-a7f8-57b5-bfd8-36f4ca12b320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485198} {:answer/id #uuid "be6becf1-5606-59ec-9b96-0f266a1a82d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485226} {:answer/id #uuid "ce0c7e1d-bae0-5c82-81a4-18c4d6be60dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be6becf1-5606-59ec-9b96-0f266a1a82d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485226} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec35b09d-4f30-50dc-a52b-44c7b5d9523b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "340e44da-12e6-5ccb-a96a-bc97b2d0d915" :question/math-academy-id "q-41706" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ in $Ax=b$ given that the matrix $A$ is orthogonal, and \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nHence, since $A$ is orthogonal, we have ${A}^{-1}={A}^{T}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}Ax & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da20ffe7-173b-5fc0-8629-3b9b70222860" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4b8b9d2-089a-5dba-b6ab-2370cafe71c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448690} {:answer/id #uuid "74213575-ddc8-5213-b2ce-a59e501dc1ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74213575-ddc8-5213-b2ce-a59e501dc1ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448691} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cebde04-2f8f-5849-8618-d6c2a4e0afbc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49fafbe7-10fb-5c34-b26c-5b9891c6d338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448692} {:answer/id #uuid "041b9065-8c9f-5ab2-b38c-d4d4aa44d1c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "041b9065-8c9f-5ab2-b38c-d4d4aa44d1c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448693} :answer-field/id #uuid "4867348a-6919-5bb7-95d2-3a16f8877ca0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449386} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a7cf8c7-d729-5add-8df3-4fe73a945535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448694} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f0d748-cf94-5065-86a9-c7923f501c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a7cf8c7-d729-5add-8df3-4fe73a945535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448694} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e31e2bd-4923-5578-a451-2148c2c56f5a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "14d8b1c2-9248-513d-b061-309a07f2a6a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-47458" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the orthogonal matrix $Q?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${Q}^{T}$ is orthogonal\n- **II.** The identity matrix $I$ is orthogonal\n- **III.** $2Q$ is orthogonal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the product ${Q}^{T}\\cdot ({Q}^{T})^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{T}\\cdot ({Q}^{T})^{T} & ={Q}^{T}Q \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The columns of the identity matrix are orthonormal. Therefore, $I$ is an orthogonal matrix.\n\n- Statement III is false. Computing the product $2Q\\cdot (2Q)^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2Q\\cdot (2Q)^{T} & =2Q\\cdot 2{Q}^{T} \\\\  & =4Q{Q}^{T} \\\\  & =4I \\\\  & \\ne I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354294 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133949 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee00be0e-f6a2-5269-a36d-1eeaf1b32344" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Product of Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a47111d-6c23-5b0a-91f9-9bb04923dabf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25-\\sqrt{33}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351802} {:answer/id #uuid "29ce09dc-21df-5eb3-a895-49c7aebe4105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351952} {:answer/id #uuid "2f429717-4c5f-5e0a-a416-5943a1f7e75a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352002} {:answer/id #uuid "b67b2975-b129-51c2-a7fa-c3fb89bbbec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353132} {:answer/id #uuid "d1b042d5-c51b-5d9e-a235-9626ad575cff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b67b2975-b129-51c2-a7fa-c3fb89bbbec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353132} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed11a05b-d987-571f-866e-9395d8d74355" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca01bd52-5594-59b2-b1c6-fbcc08e19094" :question/math-academy-id "q-84242" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}5 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4\\sqrt{2} & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|5\\cdot 5-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{2}| \\\\  & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485516 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133949 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee00be0e-f6a2-5269-a36d-1eeaf1b32344" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Product of Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cad6cbc-ec6f-5cde-bd6b-8dd94c36f1fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484843} {:answer/id #uuid "40f7c1f0-934d-531d-8563-3b0435fd55ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484960} {:answer/id #uuid "543c8564-bbcd-578e-9f7c-a13e39ae76f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485004} {:answer/id #uuid "5d6e869f-259c-5848-8df0-181caf97283c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485025} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf1b543-ec9d-55dc-86b7-270d6a4b27a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40f7c1f0-934d-531d-8563-3b0435fd55ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484960} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef0c785-702b-5715-b3a0-24d72749f491" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36bba55d-9122-58f3-aa1e-57a8674f5e02" :question/math-academy-id "q-84245" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{18}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{18}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{18}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{18}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{8} \\\\ \\sqrt{8} & 4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\sqrt{8}| \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da20ffe7-173b-5fc0-8629-3b9b70222860" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb81d4ca-b624-5bd6-b5d6-8848a582c1a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451851} {:answer/id #uuid "072d8636-45df-522c-a21c-11c80be3c9aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "072d8636-45df-522c-a21c-11c80be3c9aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451852} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ead3048-fa8d-5561-beeb-c20e86a46f07" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452773} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19f8ac0c-f828-5cbe-b1a1-9ac2fe52a581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451853} {:answer/id #uuid "78608524-9f24-5352-8c0a-c522e7bb20f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19f8ac0c-f828-5cbe-b1a1-9ac2fe52a581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451853} :answer-field/id #uuid "416ea6c4-aa3e-5622-ad1a-5f5c04bbc3f8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa1ef54f-6746-5e13-8812-1a43c4af52f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451855} {:answer/id #uuid "258461fb-779d-533f-b3c8-2a096b2dcdc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "258461fb-779d-533f-b3c8-2a096b2dcdc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451856} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bed2a41-9fc5-5095-9e22-bb769fd4e778" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6582765-66f3-5651-9e94-833ca793221c" :question/math-academy-id "q-84347" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the orthogonal matrix $P?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${P}^{T}$ is orthogonal\n- **II.** ${P}^{-1}$ is **not** orthogonal\n- **III.** $-P$ is orthogonal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the product ${P}^{T}\\cdot ({P}^{T})^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\cdot ({P}^{T})^{T} & ={P}^{T}\\cdot P \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the product ${P}^{-1}\\cdot ({P}^{-1})^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{-1}\\cdot ({P}^{-1})^{T} & ={P}^{T}\\cdot ({P}^{T})^{T} \\\\  & ={P}^{T}P \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Computing the product $(-P)\\cdot (-P)^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-P)\\cdot (-P)^{T} & =(-P)\\cdot (-{P}^{T}) \\\\  & =P{P}^{T} \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354335 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133949 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee00be0e-f6a2-5269-a36d-1eeaf1b32344" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Product of Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09afd030-d523-5b84-b318-b7f9daa2d4fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351650} {:answer/id #uuid "23ce1a71-450b-582b-aba9-d4c9c5378632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351892} {:answer/id #uuid "83459103-ad6d-52dd-9171-fbd36f5eccd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352714} {:answer/id #uuid "934a1a17-1804-55a3-a25a-8e863d3f52e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352843} {:answer/id #uuid "d8935925-a13d-5330-babc-5c8208927e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09afd030-d523-5b84-b318-b7f9daa2d4fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351650} :answer-field/id #uuid "aac9bbfd-da1f-5dc0-a202-5eb96f0371fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "821d4670-7f65-59e3-8def-f1e5c07f50f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-84778" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} & \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4\\sqrt{5} & 5\\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." :question/worked-solution "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|2\\sqrt{7}\\cdot 5\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{5}| \\\\  & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133950 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a22cfc-9a78-57ab-93a4-3c3255c34bf7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Inverse of an Orthogonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09dcffe0-ee7a-5e63-8278-dca38632fe98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{10} & -\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\sqrt{10} & -\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351652} {:answer/id #uuid "20da2b06-38a4-5f6f-bd3b-23e027784978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{10} & \\sqrt{10} \\\\ -\\sqrt{10} & -\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351862} {:answer/id #uuid "3c0842ed-cdfa-501d-926c-0f64071688a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352124} {:answer/id #uuid "a960c5de-6970-5dbc-9644-409ecdc07fdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$D$ is not invertible" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353004} {:answer/id #uuid "effacf4a-06ee-5f96-940d-3f6cb94b7ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "effacf4a-06ee-5f96-940d-3f6cb94b7ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353655} :answer-field/id #uuid "6417dc6c-e541-5ba1-aeb0-7ae4aea638c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f1af0b2-5114-5eff-85ec-5880244e7da3" :question/math-academy-id "q-84780" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the orthogonal matrix $D=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nTherefore, since $D$ is orthogonal, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{-1} & ={D}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133951 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da20ffe7-173b-5fc0-8629-3b9b70222860" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonal Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c437605-0d0b-5911-8b6f-efde64e63238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484907} {:answer/id #uuid "4b086b6e-3f56-53aa-ab01-3ec1ea51c4f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484982} {:answer/id #uuid "7328d2ac-ec4a-5f15-8f58-faebd2e52167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485064} {:answer/id #uuid "7663b203-9ab4-5d32-b8ff-e2d87fc22238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485070} {:answer/id #uuid "9697230b-8f6a-5224-a0f4-267b300f27ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c437605-0d0b-5911-8b6f-efde64e63238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484907} :answer-field/id #uuid "048ab02b-a33b-534b-a1c7-2bf319cf0b58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "35c37699-f2ab-5493-8b62-dd508d98be99" :question/math-academy-id "q-84784" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the $n\\times n$ orthogonal matrices $P$ and $Q?$\n\nI. If $A=PB{P}^{-1}$ then $|det(A)|=|det(B)|$\n\nII. $PQ$ is always orthogonal\n\nIII. $2P+Q$ is **not** always orthogonal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $Q$ is orthogonal if and only if\n\n$$\nQ{Q}^{T}={Q}^{T}Q=I.\n$$\n\nTo check that a matrix is orthogonal, it is sufficient to check that the above equation is satisfied.\n\nMoreover, we have the following properties:\n\n- For any orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we have ${Q}^{-1}={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $(AB)^{T}={B}^{T}{A}^{T}$ for conformable matrices $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing $|det(A)|,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(A)| & =|det(PB{P}^{-1})| \\\\  & =|det(PB{P}^{T})| \\\\  & =|det(P)|\\cdot |det(B)|\\cdot |det({P}^{T})| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |det(B)|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =|det(B)|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the product $(PQ)\\cdot (PQ)^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ\\cdot (PQ)^{T} & =(PQ)\\cdot {Q}^{T}{P}^{T} \\\\  & =P(Q{Q}^{T}){P}^{T} \\\\  & =P(I){P}^{T} \\\\  & =P{P}^{T} \\\\  & =I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. As a counterexample, consider the following sum involving two orthogonal matrices:\n\n$$\n2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe resulting matrix is not orthogonal since, for example, the first column is not normalized.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}]}
